# Inherits everything from the root .clang-tidy and turns off the checks that
# only misfire here. Tests are held to the same standard otherwise: this list
# is for false positives, not for letting test code rot.
#
#   bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
#     REQUIRE(x.has_value()) throws when it fails, so the *x on the next line
#     is safe. clang-tidy does not model Catch2's macros and reports every
#     one of them.
#
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#     Catch2's macros expand into branches, so a test with a handful of
#     CHECKs scores like a function with a handful of ifs.
#
# Tests also leave fields out of designated initializers, which is valid C++
# and lets a test name only what it is about. Clang warns about that, and /WX
# in the compile database makes the warning an error that stops the analysis
# of the file, so ExtraArgs turns it off. src/ lists every field and keeps it.

InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
ExtraArgs:
  - -Wno-missing-designated-field-initializers
